---
title: Reading a home timeline — the hybrid merge
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User (browser)
    participant G as gateway
    participant TL as timeline-service
    participant R as Redis
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant T as tweet-service

    U->>G: GET /api/v1/timeline?limit=50
    G->>G: validate JWT, check rate limit
    G->>TL: forward (subject = userId)

    par precomputed portion
        TL->>R: LRANGE timeline:{userId} 0 49
        R-->>TL: tweet IDs from non-celebrity authors
    and celebrity portion
        TL->>R: SMEMBERS celebrities ∩ following:{userId}
        R-->>TL: celebrity author IDs (small set)
        TL->>DB: SELECT id FROM tweets<br/>WHERE author_id IN (...)<br/>AND created_at > now() - interval '2 days'<br/>ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 50
        DB-->>TL: recent celebrity tweet IDs
    end

    TL->>TL: merge both lists by UUIDv7 order, take 50
    TL->>T: GET /internal/tweets?ids=...  (hydrate)
    T-->>TL: tweet bodies, media keys, stats
    TL-->>G: timeline page
    G-->>U: 200 OK

    Note over TL,DB: If Redis is unavailable the precomputed branch is skipped<br/>and the whole timeline is rebuilt from PostgreSQL:<br/>slower, but correct. Nothing durable lives in Redis.
